DATA TYPES in SQL
  INT - for integers stored in table
  VARCHAR - variable string 
  ENUM - string object value chosen from list of permitted value 
  DATE - stores date value

  TIMESTAMPS - Stores Date and Time , automatically set to current 
  BOOLEAN - True or False
  DECIMAL - (10,2) exact values (total number of digits, digits after decimal)


  CONSTARINTS 
  1 . Auto_increment - Automatically generates a unique number for each row.
  2. Primary key - uniquely identifies each row in the table
  3. not null - ensures a column cannot have a null value 
  4. unique - ensures all values in a column are different
  
